  "holistic_F_N": 0,
  "holistic_F_H": 0,
  "section_notes": "S1 imposes strict 24-hour reporting and 48-hour customer notice, with reporting required despite cause uncertainty. S2 requires a 55°C test and a 5% threshold but no automatic sales stop, and gives per-model results to purchasers/regulators without public publication. S3 requires new-unit shut-off and a 6-year retrofit with feasibility alternatives; S4 requires built-in suppression at 36 months but allows a validated equivalent; S5 sets an 8/100k review trigger but makes recall discretionary based on a regulator risk determination."
